[ ADVANCED: AUTO-CHAINING (COMMANDER) ]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To setup a Commander chain without manual timers:
    local cancel = TDS:AutoChain(1, 2, 3)

The script automatically detects timescale:
• At 1x speed: Waits 10.5 seconds between activations.
• At 2x speed: Waits 5.5 seconds between activations.
Call `cancel()` to terminate the chain at any wave.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ADVANCED: INFINITE LOOP (Autoexec) ]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For 24/7 AFK, place your strategy script into your executor's 'autoexec' folder.
Whenever a match completes:
1. If `AutoRestart = true`: The script votes restart directly on the rewards screen.
2. If `AutoRejoin = true`: The script teleports back to the lobby, replays matchmaking,
   and automatically resumes execution from 'ADS_LastStrat.lua'.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ADVANCED: POSITIONING (dist / pointToEnd) ]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The "dist" parameter controls WHERE on the path the ability triggers.

• 0 = The START of the road (where enemies spawn).
• The higher the number, the further down the road the ability targets.
• Each map has a different maximum distance (Simplicity is ~156).

HOW TO FIND VALUES FOR OTHER MAPS:
1. Open a RemoteSpy (e.g. SimpleSpy or Hydroxide).
2. Activate the Ability manually in-game.
3. Look for the 'RemoteFunction' call named "Troops" with action "Abilities".
4. Check the 'Data' table in the spy log to see the exact 'dist' value.

NOTE: If you set the value to 999, the unit/airstrike will target the 
very end of the path or remain stuck at the exit until it times out.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ TROUBLESHOOTING & TIPS ]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
• ERROR "No HTTP Function": Your executor does not support 'request'. Use a
  supported executor with standard sUNC compatibility.
• TOWERS NOT PLACING: Ensure you have enough cash. The engine will retry 
  automatically, but cannot place towers if your balance is insufficient.
• INDEXING: Towers are indexed in the order they are placed (1, 2, 3...). If 
  you sell Index 1, Index 2 remains 2; it does not shift down.
• LOADOUT EQUIPPING: Always use `TDS:Loadout("Tower1", "Tower2", ...)` rather 
  than individual equip calls. It handles unequipping and re-equipping cleanly.
• WEBHOOKS: Ensure `getgenv().WebhookURL` is your full Discord webhook URL. If 
  left empty or invalid, the script will skip sending results.

